course: dictionary
lesson: 9093
title: One word, many meanings: slur
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context shows you which one the writer means. The word slur has four meanings, so read the sentence around it and look for clues.
explain: To slur means to say words unclearly, so the sounds run together. «At pick-up, Liam-Jay's mum is stumbling and slurring.» Stumbling is a clue: the words are blurred, so slurring must mean speaking unclearly.
explain: A slur can also be an insult, a remark that damages someone's good name, as in «a slur on his good name». A slur can also be a hurtful word aimed at a group of people, for example because of their race, religion or disability. That is bullying, and it should always be reported.
explain: In music, a slur is a curved line over notes. It tells you to play or sing those notes smoothly together. There is no word to read at all, so the context is the picture, not the words.
fact: «Slur» can be a noun (a slur) or a verb (to slur).
fact: «Slurred speech» means words that are unclear, with the sounds running together.
fact: Slurred speech can be a warning sign of a stroke, so get help fast and call emergency services.
fact: «A racial slur» is a nasty, hurtful word used against a group of people; using slurs is bullying and should be reported.
fact: In music, a slur is a smooth curve over notes.
exercise: «Shivering hard, pale skin, slurred speech and being very sleepy can be signs a person is getting dangerously cold.» What does slurred speech mean here? | Singing in a high voice | Shouting very loudly | *Words that are unclear, with the sounds running together
exercise: A curved line over notes tells you to play them smoothly. What is that line called? | A tempo | *A slur | A rest | A sharp
exercise: «A slur on his good name» is a phrase. What does slur mean here? | Speech that is very slow | A kind compliment | A smooth curve over notes | *An insult that damages someone's reputation
test: What is the name for the body getting dangerously cold? | Hyperactivity | Hibernation | *Hypothermia
test: A hurtful word used against a group of people is a slur. What should you do about it? | Ignore it forever | Laugh with the bullies | *Report it | Repeat it to your friends
exam: Which meaning fits «a slur on someone's character»? | *An insult that damages someone's reputation | A curved line over notes | Speaking very slowly | A warning sign of the cold
